{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-8060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-8060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection in the line $y=-x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-8060" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d34a683a99f73da8e108a2adc1ffc3b9494199f40acb9dee495670bab043603e"} {"question" "q-8060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-8060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Dilation with scale factor $1$"] ["text" "Reflection across the $x$-axis"] ["text" "Reflection across the $y$-axis"] ["text" "Reflection in the line $y=-x$"] ["text" "Reflection in the line $y=x$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-8060" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Reflection in the line $y=-x$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-11952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-11952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that a dilation of scale factor $k$ is represented by the matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nHere, we have $k=2.$ Therefore, the matrix represents a dilation with a scale factor of $2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-11952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d34a683a99f73da8e108a2adc1ffc3b9494199f40acb9dee495670bab043603e"} {"question" "q-11952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-11952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Dilation with scale factor $2$"] ["text" "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$"] ["text" "Reflection across the $x$-axis"] ["text" "Reflection in the line $x=2$"] ["text" "Reflection in the line $y=x$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-11952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Dilation with scale factor $2$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-78294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}60 \\\\ 144\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-78294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}60 \\\\ 144\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{12}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{12}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-78294" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d34a683a99f73da8e108a2adc1ffc3b9494199f40acb9dee495670bab043603e"} {"question" "q-78294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-78294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{12} \\\\ \\frac{1}{12} & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}12 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 1 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-78294" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{12} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-159762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What linear transformation $T$ is represented by the matrix $T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-159762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we compute the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/assets/dbe3773dea369f6b58fc2ad45a32f98c2c9ae356701baf3ab56af3daa6ca732d.png)\n\nTherefore, the matrix represents a reflection across the $x$-axis." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-159762" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d34a683a99f73da8e108a2adc1ffc3b9494199f40acb9dee495670bab043603e"} {"question" "q-159762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-159762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "Dilation with scale factor $-1$"] ["text" "Reflection across the $x$-axis"] ["text" "Reflection across the $y$-axis"] ["text" "Reflection in the line $y=-x$"] ["text" "Reflection in the line $y=x$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-159762" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Reflection across the $x$-axis"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{5}{3}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{5}{3}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d34a683a99f73da8e108a2adc1ffc3b9494199f40acb9dee495670bab043603e"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{5}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"question" "q-328229" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070817/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bbb2a1bf48119a9200533da93761991c52db7aca497b3996fe3052689963ccf"} {"questi